bic_trace_step.reason:
The vulnerability is present in the cleanup loop at the end of the `setup_nic_devices()` function. The code shows:

c
setup_nic_wait_intr:

	while (i--) {
		dev_err(&octeon_dev->pci_dev->dev,
			"NIC ifidx:%d Setup failed\n", i);
		liquidio_destroy_nic_device(octeon_dev, i);
	}
	return -ENODEV;


The loop uses `while(i--)` which decrements `i` BEFORE processing the current iteration. When the initialization loop fails at index `i`, the cleanup jumps to `setup_nic_wait_intr` label. The `while(i--)` then immediately decrements `i` again before the first cleanup iteration, causing the element at the failing index to be skipped and not freed. For example, if failure occurs at i=2, the loop will decrement to i=1 before the first iteration, skipping cleanup of index 2. The correct pattern should be `while(i--)` starting from the last successfully initialized index, but the current code structure causes an off-by-one error in the cleanup sequence.
